# System Design Study Canvases — build recipe

You are building **interactive HTML study canvases** for system-design interview prep.
Everything is self-contained, offline, and prints to PDF (Cmd/Ctrl+P). No build step.

## Where things live
```
canvas/
  index.html                 hub grid (foundations + 20 use-case tiles)
  assets/canvas.css          shared design system + interactive-layer styles
  assets/canvas.js           vanilla JS interactivity (see hooks below)
  assets/logos/{aws,gcp,azure}.svg     provider brand logos
  assets/logos/services/*.svg          per-service icons (ONLY use ones that exist)
  f1-cap-consistency.html  f2-must-know-algorithms.html  f3-estimation-numbers.html
  NN-slug/{hld,lld,deepdive}.html      one folder per use case, 3 canvases each
```
Canvas HTML files reference assets via `../assets/...` (foundations are flat, use `assets/...`).

## Status
- **DONE (20/20):** all foundations F1–F3 and every use case 01–20 have HLD + LLD + Deep-dive canvases.
- The last batch (14 real-time collab, 16 stock trading, 17 task scheduler, 18 observability) was built
  on the mandatory 3-col × 6/7-row spacious grid (see Rule A below). Older canvases still use the
  legacy 4-col grid — do NOT retrofit them without a specific bug report.

## The exemplar — ALWAYS copy its structure
`canvas/01-url-shortener/{hld,lld,deepdive}.html` is the reference. Match its layout, class
names, section order, and interactive wiring exactly. Do not invent a new structure.

## Grounding — read the real project docs before writing
For use case `NN-slug`, read that project's `NN-slug/docs/{hld,lld,patterns,tradeoffs,caching,tech,cloud}/`,
its `NN-slug/revision/`, and `NN-slug/src/` (real Java classes). Every claim, class name, and
algorithm on a canvas must be grounded in those files — not invented.

## Each use case = 3 canvases
1. **hld.html** — functional/non-functional requirements, estimation chips, an interactive SVG
   architecture diagram with clickable `[data-node]` components (each reveals a `.node-detail`),
   a numbered write/read `.flow` stepper (arrows numbered 1..N, no gaps/dupes), and a cloud
   mapping `table.cloudtable` (columns: Component | AWS | GCP | Azure; provider logos in headers,
   per-service `svcicon` `<img>` on white chips).
2. **lld.html** — clickable class map of the REAL Java classes, core algorithm in
   `<pre class="code">`, tabs/collapsibles, and a "Run it" file map.
3. **deepdive.html** — scaling tabs, bottleneck collapsibles, CAP analysis, a trade-offs table,
   and an interview-walkthrough timing strip.

Every canvas ends with `§ Glossary — one-liners` and a walkthrough footer nav.

## JS interactive hooks (already in assets/canvas.js — wire the HTML to these)
Use the EXACT attribute names below — the JS reads these literal strings. Any deviation
(e.g. `data-tabpanel` instead of `data-panel`) silently breaks the click handler.

- **Tabs:** MUST use this exact 3-level structure:
  ```html
  <div data-tabscope>              <!-- WRAPPER — data-tabscope goes HERE, NOT on .tabs -->
    <div class="tabs">
      <button class="tab active" data-tab="alpha">…</button>
      <button class="tab"        data-tab="beta">…</button>
    </div>
    <div class="tabpanel active" data-panel="alpha">…</div>
    <div class="tabpanel"        data-panel="beta">…</div>
  </div>
  ```
  Rules: (a) `data-tabscope` on the OUTER wrapper that contains BOTH `.tabs` and the panels —
  never on the `.tabs` element itself (breaks `closest('[data-tabscope]')` panel lookup).
  (b) every `data-tab` on a `<button>` MUST equal a `data-panel` on a sibling `.tabpanel`
  (attribute is `data-panel`, not `data-tabpanel`). (c) exactly one `.tab.active` and one
  `.tabpanel.active` per group for the initial state.
- **Collapsibles:** `<div class="card collapsible">` → child `<div class="c-head">` (clickable header)
  + `<div class="c-body">` (content). Add `open` on the card to start expanded.
- **Diagram:** `<svg class="arch">` (or wrap in `<div class="arch">`) with clickable groups
  `<g data-node data-title="…" data-detail="… HTML …">`; a sibling `<div class="node-detail">`
  with `<span class="nd-title">` and `<div class="nd-body">` receives the content.
- **Flow stepper:** wrap the section in `[data-flowscope]`. Arrows: `<line class="arrow" data-flow="produce" data-produce="N" data-desc-produce="…">`.
  Controls: `<div data-flowctl>` with `<button data-flow="produce">` path buttons and
  `<button data-flowstep="prev">` / `data-flowstep="next"` step buttons. Optional
  `<div data-flowlabel>` shows the current step's description.
- **Estimator / converter:** IDs `est-dau`, `est-actions`, `est-rw`, `est-payload`, `est-retention`
  → outputs `o-writesday`, `o-readsday`, `o-wqps`, `o-rqps`, `o-tqps`, `o-peak`, `o-storeday`,
  `o-storetotal`, `o-bw`. Converter: `cv-val`, `cv-unit`, `cv-B..cv-PB`, `[data-base="1024|1000"]`.

**Symptoms → likely causes:**
- Tab click does nothing ⇒ (1) `data-tabpanel` instead of `data-panel` on the panel, OR
  (2) `data-tabscope` sits on the `.tabs` element itself instead of a wrapper containing both
  `.tabs` and the panels — `tabs.closest('[data-tabscope]')` then returns the tabs div and no
  panels are found inside it.
- Node click doesn't reveal detail ⇒ `.node-detail` is not a sibling of the `.arch` container.
- Flow "Next ▶" does nothing ⇒ arrow is missing `data-<pathName>="N"`, or arrow is outside the
  `[data-flowscope]` section.

