## SVG diagram layout — HARD RULES (no overlaps, no orphans)

Every clickable SVG diagram (HLD architecture map, LLD class map) MUST follow these rules.
Violations produce hidden boxes, mystery-orphan nodes, and unreadable canvases.

### Rule A — Spacious 3-column grid (PRIMARY layout for all new canvases)

**Default grid for HLD + LLD (use this unless you have a strong reason not to):**
  - viewBox: `0 0 900 520` (6 rows) or `0 0 900 560` (7 rows). Widen height, not width — the
    hub's `max-width:900` keeps everything readable.
  - **3 columns × wide nodes:**
    - Col 1: `x=20`, width **240** → ends at x=260
    - Col 2: `x=330`, width **240** → ends at x=570
    - Col 3: `x=640`, width **240** → ends at x=880
  - **70 px gutters** at x=260-330 and x=570-640 — real breathing room for labels + L-paths.
  - **Rows:** stride 80 (6-row grid) or stride 75 (7-row grid). Node height 54.
    - 6-row: `y ∈ {30, 110, 190, 270, 350, 430}`, row-gaps 26 px each.
    - 7-row: `y ∈ {30, 105, 180, 255, 330, 405, 480}`, row-gaps 21 px each.
  - Font sizes: title 13, subtitle 11 (fits ~30 chars in a 240-px node). STAR node title 14.

**Why:** node subtitles fit inside the box, arrows have gutter room, arrow labels have
row-gap × gutter intersections to live in. The old 4-col (140-170 px node) grid produced
overflowing subtitles and arrow spaghetti — do not use it for new canvases.

**Subtitle length hard cap:** ≤ 28 chars at font-size 11. If longer, split into two nodes or
shorten. Grep to verify: `rg -oN 'font-size="1[01]">[^<]{29,}' canvas/NN-*/*.html` must be empty.

**Legacy 4-col grid (only for foundations f1–f3 and already-shipped use cases):**
  - Col 1: x=20 (w≤150) · Col 2: x=205 (w≤130) · Col 3: x=395 (w≤130) · Col 4: x=620 (w≤150)
  - Row grid y ∈ {26, 86, 150, 210, 270, 330 …}, height ≤ 50, ≥ 10 px gap.
  - Only used to keep old canvases stable. New canvases MUST use the 3-col grid above.

### Rule B — Explicit non-overlap check (do this BEFORE finishing)
For every pair of `<rect>` nodes, verify NO overlap:
  `x1 + w1 ≤ x2  OR  x2 + w2 ≤ x1  OR  y1 + h1 ≤ y2  OR  y2 + h2 ≤ y1`
Any pair that fails must be moved to a different column or row before you write the file.
If two nodes conceptually belong at the same coordinate, split into 2 rows or shrink one.

### Rule C — No orphan nodes (every `[data-node]` needs an arrow)
Every `<g data-node>` MUST have at least ONE `<line class="arrow">` or `<path class="arrow">`
that starts OR ends within 12 px of one of its edges. If a node exists conceptually but has
no relationship arrow, remove the node — floating boxes look like bugs, not design choices.
Include repository blocks, metadata stores, offset stores, metrics/utility boxes — no exceptions.

### Rule D — viewBox sizing
`viewBox` height MUST equal `bottom-most (y + height) + 20 px` minimum. Never let the last
row's bottom equal or exceed the viewBox height; the `.node-detail` panel will collide.

### Rule E — Arrow legibility
- Solid arrows = core wiring / request path. Dashed (`stroke-dasharray="4 3"`) = "uses / implements / references".
- Never route an arrow straight through the interior of a non-endpoint node — go around, or use a curved `<path>`.
- **Arrow labels MUST use `class="edge-label"`** (defined in `assets/canvas.css`). This applies:
  fill=`--muted`, font-size=10, and a `paint-order:stroke` halo in `--bg` — text stays legible
  even where it overlaps a node interior. Never use inline `fill="var(--faint)" font-size="9"`
  for arrow labels — old canvases still work via a compatibility selector, but new canvases
  MUST use the class.
- Position labels in **gutters** (3-col grid: x ∈ 260-330 or 570-640; legacy 4-col: x ∈ 190–220,
  390–420, 590–620) or **row-gaps** (3-col 6-row: y ∈ 84-110, 164-190, 244-270, 324-350, 404-430;
  3-col 7-row: y ∈ 84-105, 159-180, 234-255, 309-330, 384-405, 459-480). A label MUST land in a
  **gutter × row-gap intersection**, e.g. `x=295 y=177`. If it can't, **delete the label** —
  the halo is a last-resort correction, not a licence to place labels wherever. When in doubt,
  prefer **fewer, higher-value labels** (the star call + 1-2 semantically important edges) over
  labelling every arrow. Any label that only restates the arrow direction (e.g. `pricing` on
  `X → PricingStrategy`, `synchronized` on a "uses" edge, `throws` on an exception edge) is
  noise — omit it.
- **Fan-out from a saga/orchestrator to N participants:** don't try to draw N straight verticals
  that clip intermediate nodes. Route N-1 of them through the RIGHT gutter as L-paths at
  staggered x-offsets (e.g. x=595, x=615, x=625). The one directly-adjacent participant gets a
  short vertical inside the column. See `canvas/10-ecommerce/hld.html` C6/C8 for the pattern.
- Flow-stepper arrows are numbered via `data-write="N"` / `data-read="N"` — sequence 1..N with no gaps or duplicates.

### Rule F — Only use defined CSS palette vars (or the box vanishes)
Node `stroke`, `fill`, and `text fill` MUST reference a var that actually exists in `assets/canvas.css`.
The full whitelist is:
  - **Neutrals:** `--text`, `--muted`, `--faint`, `--border`, `--panel`, `--panel-2`, `--bg`
  - **Categorical:** `--eden` (teal), `--survivor` (amber), `--old` (violet), `--meta` (rose),
    `--stack` (sky), `--gc` (green), `--warn` (red), `--fig` (alias for sky — "strategies")
If you catch yourself typing a made-up name (`--accent`, `--primary`, `--engine`, `--proxy`, …),
either add it to `:root` in `canvas/assets/canvas.css` OR pick a real one. An undefined CSS var
resolves to nothing → the SVG stroke disappears and the node blends into the dark background.
**Verify before finishing:** `rg -o 'var\(--[a-z0-9-]+\)' canvas/NN-*/*.html | sort -u`,
compare against the whitelist above.

## Self-check before finishing a canvas
Run through this checklist explicitly; do not skip:
- [ ] All asset paths use `../assets/` (foundations use `assets/`).
- [ ] Every interactive hook is wired and works.
- [ ] Flow arrows numbered 1..N, no gaps/dupes.
- [ ] Every `svcicon` `src` points to a file that exists in `assets/logos/services/`.
- [ ] Java class references are real (exist in `NN-slug/src/`).
- [ ] `§ Glossary` present + footer walkthrough nav present.
- [ ] **Layout Rule A** — every node sits on the column/row grid.
- [ ] **Layout Rule B** — pairwise rect-overlap check passes for every diagram.
- [ ] **Layout Rule C** — every `[data-node]` has ≥ 1 arrow touching it (no orphans).
- [ ] **Layout Rule D** — viewBox height ≥ bottom-most node bottom + 20 px.
- [ ] **Layout Rule E** — no arrow crosses through a non-endpoint node's interior.
- [ ] **Layout Rule F** — every `var(--…)` in HLD/LLD resolves to a var defined in `assets/canvas.css`.
- [ ] **Interactivity smoke-test** — for every `.tabs` block, confirm each `data-tab` value has a
      matching `data-panel` (NOT `data-tabpanel`) inside the same `[data-tabscope]`. For every
      `[data-node]`, confirm a sibling `.node-detail` exists. For every `[data-flowctl]` path
      button, confirm at least one arrow has `data-<path>="1"` inside the same `[data-flowscope]`.
      Grep is enough: `data-tab="[^"]+"` should equal `data-panel="[^"]+"` sets.

## After building a batch
1. Wire the finished tiles into `canvas/index.html`: replace the `.tile.soon` markup with
   `<a class="tile" href="NN-slug/hld.html">…</a>` (copy a "ready" tile's markup).
2. Build one use case at a time (or one small batch), then verify in browser before moving on.
